# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A SOPS-encrypted secrets/*.sops.yaml is safe to commit; a plaintext one is not. The naming convention
# cannot tell them apart — the file has the same name either way — so gitignore alone cannot make this
# safe. These rules cover the plaintext names the docs assume, and .githooks/pre-commit covers the case
# that actually bit: a *.sops.yaml that was never encrypted.
secrets/*.plain.yaml
secrets/*.plaintext.yaml
secrets/demo-secrets.yaml
secrets/*.decrypted.yaml
